(footprint "PD_FGA01FC_EdgeBracket"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "hand")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Thorlabs FGA01FC InGaAs photodiode held by the photodiode_PCBedgeholder bracket (Bracket v5). The bracket clamps the PCB FRONT EDGE in a 1.86 mm slot and the diode flange bolts to its front face with 2x M2, so the board carries the diode and the panel only needs a clearance hole. ORIGIN = can axis projected onto the board; local +X points TOWARD the board front edge, which MUST sit at local X = +5.00 (see the F.Fab datum line). Can back face lands 1.0 mm forward of the edge. LEADS: pin 1 (K) and pin 3 (A) exit at the F.Cu surface plane at Y = +/-1.25 and lie FLAT on top - they solder to surface pads, no bend. Pin 2 (CASE) exits 1.25 mm below the axis, bends down across the 1.0 mm gap in front of the board edge, passes UNDER the board and solders to a B.Cu pad. Clocking pin 2 downward makes the flange orientation unique, which is what stops pin 1 and pin 3 being swapped. MOUNTING: 2x plated 2.2 mm holes (ISO 273 close clearance for M2 - FINISHED hole size, tell the fab) on 13.624 mm centres, 2.5 mm in from the board edge, carried as pad 2 so they land on the CASE/GND net with no schematic change. Their 4.0 x 5.0 mm mask-free lands are the metal-to-metal contact face for the conductive bracket arms - specify ENIG, a HASL bump makes a poor contact. PINOUT is fully determined by the datasheet (24112-S01 Rev F p.3) - do not re-derive it: the schematic figure puts the TRIANGLE on pin 3 and the BAR on pin 1, so pin 1 = K (cathode), pin 2 = CASE, pin 3 = A (anode). Cathode -> PDn_BIAS_K -> +12 V through R_S; anode -> PDn_IN, the TIA summing node at 0 V. The diode is therefore reverse-biased and photocurrent flows INTO the summing node, so the TIA output swings NEGATIVE from 0 V dark at -8.06 mV/uA. A swapped 1/3 would forward-bias the diode and park the stage at a rail.")
	(tags "photodiode InGaAs TO-46 FC/PC Thorlabs FGA01FC edge bracket panel mount grounded")
	(attr through_hole exclude_from_pos_files exclude_from_bom)

